{"duration_api_ms":751288,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"e451ebe5-3512-4772-b995-65bcc3c3c64b","total_cost_usd":3.4113418,"usage":{"input_tokens":200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":130060,"cache_read_input_tokens":11180309,"output_tokens":65464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":36651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":130060,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3176,"cache_read_input_tokens":153249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1142},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":200,"outputTokens":65464,"cacheReadInputTokens":11180309,"cacheCreationInputTokens":130060,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.4113418,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":36651,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":129,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured node1 (VyOS) as a NAT gateway for the private \\\"lan\\\" network (10.50.50.0/24, egress:false) so node2 and node3 can reach the internet through it, implemented via an idempotent Ansible playbook run from control_node node4. node1's eth1 got a static LAN address plus a source-NAT masquerade rule outbound on eth0; node2/node3's enp8s0 got static LAN IPs plus source-based policy routing (ip rule + custom table 200 via NetworkManager) so traffic sourced from their private LAN address routes through node1, while their separate mgmt-network default route (used for cluster/exec connectivity) is left untouched. Verified via ping/curl from the LAN addresses and conntrack/nft masquerade counters on node1. Also fixed a VyOS SSH-key persistence issue (authorized_keys is regenerated from declarative config on boot) by adding the ansible key via `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`. All four nodes were restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol; boot_id changes were captured for each and NAT/routing/connectivity were reverified as fully recovered and persistent after every restart, with a final idempotent (all-ok, zero-changed) Ansible run confirming durable configuration.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS (mgmt+lan NICs), node2/node3=CentOS Stream 10 (mgmt+lan NICs), node4=ansible-controller (mgmt only); confirmed via environment.toml that control_node=node4 and 'lan' network has dhcp=false, egress=false\",\"Set up passwordless SSH from node4 to node1 (vyos user) and node2/node3 (root) using CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/PUBKEY\",\"Diagnosed a VyOS non-interactive config-session quirk (bash alias expansion across semicolon-joined lines, and cli-shell-api session-ownership under a non-root user) and resolved it by running config blocks as `sudo -n bash -c '...'` with real newlines between commands\",\"Wrote /root/ansible/nat-egress/{inventory.ini,nat-egress.yml} on node4: play 1 sets node1 eth1's static LAN address and a NAT source masquerade rule via raw VyOS commands; play 2 uses community.general.nmcli on node2/node3 to set a static LAN IP plus a source-based ip-rule/route-table (table 200) default route via node1, with never_default4 so the mgmt default route is untouched\",\"Ran the playbook from node4 and validated NAT egress end-to-end with ping/curl sourced from the LAN addresses plus conntrack/nft masquerade counters on node1; confirmed a second playbook run was fully idempotent (ok=.., changed=0 everywhere)\",\"Fixed persistence of the ansible-controller's SSH key on node1 by adding it through VyOS's declarative `system login user vyos authentication public-keys` config (raw authorized_keys edits are regenerated/wiped by VyOS on boot)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baselines on all four nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3, and node4 one at a time (native reboot mechanisms), polling each until exec was available again and confirming a changed boot_id for each\",\"After each restart, reverified NAT config, policy routes, and internet reachability from node2/node3's LAN addresses recovered, and after the last restart (node4) reran the Ansible playbook to confirm persistence and idempotency of the full deployment\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 configured with NAT (LAN address + source masquerade rule) via Ansible\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8146728532d24280\",\"cmd-eaa37b1767624921\",\"cmd-8c10bb7b07e54afe\",\"cmd-45a53e4ea2cc40b0\",\"cmd-1c4358ca5f1c450c\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS eth1 static address 10.50.50.254/24 and NAT source rule 100 (masquerade out eth0 for 10.50.50.0/24) applied and confirmed via config.boot/nft ruleset; final ansible-playbook run shows node1 ok=1 changed=0 (idempotent)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured (via Ansible) with LAN addresses and routing through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0afa6f52abec43af\",\"cmd-12b7bc50d59947ee\",\"cmd-1c4358ca5f1c450c\"],\"summary\":\"nmcli-managed static LAN IPs (10.50.50.11/12) with ip rule + table 200 default route via 10.50.50.254 applied through the playbook; final playbook run shows node2/node3 ok=1 changed=0\"},{\"requirement\":\"Processes on node2/node3 can actually reach the internet through node1's NAT\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-12b7bc50d59947ee\",\"cmd-3c76b7542b9b4133\",\"cmd-ee08992dd22546a9\",\"cmd-277641cfb99949fc\",\"cmd-844f0c73bc804101\"],\"summary\":\"ping/curl sourced from 10.50.50.11 and 10.50.50.12 succeed (HTTP 301, ICMP replies); node1's conntrack table shows the flows translated to node1's WAN IP 10.100.23.10 and nft masquerade rule counters incrementing\"},{\"requirement\":\"mgmt/control-plane connectivity on node2/node3 left intact (not disrupted by the LAN routing change)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0afa6f52abec43af\",\"cmd-b54f6b38c9894cc6\",\"cmd-ae327d419d7844a3\"],\"summary\":\"ip route show default on node2/node3 continues to show the original DHCP default via enp1s0/10.100.23.1 unchanged after configuration and after reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implemented using Ansible from the designated control_node\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4604e4fbddf446e1\",\"cmd-baff03e26a434bfe\",\"cmd-f640e0d1ed8243b7\",\"cmd-45a53e4ea2cc40b0\",\"cmd-4c1c9b88b5954762\"],\"summary\":\"Inventory and playbook created on node4 (control_node per environment.toml) and run with ansible-playbook; two consecutive runs show correct application then full idempotency\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2f20e5428e0b402f\",\"cmd-650e575226ab4735\",\"cmd-13252d95be074f74\",\"cmd-59ce97d89c344c4f\",\"cmd-2baf9552a4dd49ad\",\"cmd-c097c819b5cd4146\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 01e92881...; reboot acknowledged and node timed out; post-reboot boot_id ae3c5761... (changed); eth1/NAT config and node2/node3 connectivity through node1 confirmed recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-68634265eda4491d\",\"cmd-62200db073654ae8\",\"cmd-e0e46cb2aa934683\",\"cmd-b54f6b38c9894cc6\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2c237d4f...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id 26f968dc... (changed); LAN IP, ip rule/table 200, and internet reachability via node1 confirmed recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bcac387313194147\",\"cmd-3205ef0e1b9446b8\",\"cmd-a685438036f849c6\",\"cmd-ae327d419d7844a3\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 5b620f5a...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id 6e547ff0... (changed); LAN IP, ip rule/table 200, and internet reachability via node1 confirmed recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 mandatory restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-514b5bb1e4ad43e5\",\"cmd-0aefa57dac1a483d\",\"cmd-cb7c35bd7e624cce\",\"cmd-0f3fe61b02c84a45\",\"cmd-1c4358ca5f1c450c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e796da36...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id c07d00e7... (changed); ansible artifacts intact and a full playbook re-run from node4 succeeded idempotently, confirming orchestration capability recovered\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (VyOS) as a NAT gateway for the private \"lan\" network (10.50.50.0/24, egress:false) so node2 and node3 can reach the internet through it, implemented via an idempotent Ansible playbook run from control_node node4. node1's eth1 got a static LAN address plus a source-NAT masquerade rule outbound on eth0; node2/node3's enp8s0 got static LAN IPs plus source-based policy routing (ip rule + custom table 200 via NetworkManager) so traffic sourced from their private LAN address routes through node1, while their separate mgmt-network default route (used for cluster/exec connectivity) is left untouched. Verified via ping/curl from the LAN addresses and conntrack/nft masquerade counters on node1. Also fixed a VyOS SSH-key persistence issue (authorized_keys is regenerated from declarative config on boot) by adding the ansible key via `set system login user vyos authentication public-keys`. All four nodes were restarted one at a time per the mandatory protocol; boot_id changes were captured for each and NAT/routing/connectivity were reverified as fully recovered and persistent after every restart, with a final idempotent (all-ok, zero-changed) Ansible run confirming durable configuration.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS (mgmt+lan NICs), node2/node3=CentOS Stream 10 (mgmt+lan NICs), node4=ansible-controller (mgmt only); confirmed via environment.toml that control_node=node4 and 'lan' network has dhcp=false, egress=false","Set up passwordless SSH from node4 to node1 (vyos user) and node2/node3 (root) using CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/PUBKEY","Diagnosed a VyOS non-interactive config-session quirk (bash alias expansion across semicolon-joined lines, and cli-shell-api session-ownership under a non-root user) and resolved it by running config blocks as `sudo -n bash -c '...'` with real newlines between commands","Wrote /root/ansible/nat-egress/{inventory.ini,nat-egress.yml} on node4: play 1 sets node1 eth1's static LAN address and a NAT source masquerade rule via raw VyOS commands; play 2 uses community.general.nmcli on node2/node3 to set a static LAN IP plus a source-based ip-rule/route-table (table 200) default route via node1, with never_default4 so the mgmt default route is untouched","Ran the playbook from node4 and validated NAT egress end-to-end with ping/curl sourced from the LAN addresses plus conntrack/nft masquerade counters on node1; confirmed a second playbook run was fully idempotent (ok=.., changed=0 everywhere)","Fixed persistence of the ansible-controller's SSH key on node1 by adding it through VyOS's declarative `system login user vyos authentication public-keys` config (raw authorized_keys edits are regenerated/wiped by VyOS on boot)","Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime baselines on all four nodes, then restarted node1, node2, node3, and node4 one at a time (native reboot mechanisms), polling each until exec was available again and confirming a changed boot_id for each","After each restart, reverified NAT config, policy routes, and internet reachability from node2/node3's LAN addresses recovered, and after the last restart (node4) reran the Ansible playbook to confirm persistence and idempotency of the full deployment"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 configured with NAT (LAN address + source masquerade rule) via Ansible","command_ids":["cmd-8146728532d24280","cmd-eaa37b1767624921","cmd-8c10bb7b07e54afe","cmd-45a53e4ea2cc40b0","cmd-1c4358ca5f1c450c"],"summary":"VyOS eth1 static address 10.50.50.254/24 and NAT source rule 100 (masquerade out eth0 for 10.50.50.0/24) applied and confirmed via config.boot/nft ruleset; final ansible-playbook run shows node1 ok=1 changed=0 (idempotent)"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured (via Ansible) with LAN addresses and routing through node1","command_ids":["cmd-0afa6f52abec43af","cmd-12b7bc50d59947ee","cmd-1c4358ca5f1c450c"],"summary":"nmcli-managed static LAN IPs (10.50.50.11/12) with ip rule + table 200 default route via 10.50.50.254 applied through the playbook; final playbook run shows node2/node3 ok=1 changed=0"},{"requirement":"Processes on node2/node3 can actually reach the internet through node1's NAT","command_ids":["cmd-12b7bc50d59947ee","cmd-3c76b7542b9b4133","cmd-ee08992dd22546a9","cmd-277641cfb99949fc","cmd-844f0c73bc804101"],"summary":"ping/curl sourced from 10.50.50.11 and 10.50.50.12 succeed (HTTP 301, ICMP replies); node1's conntrack table shows the flows translated to node1's WAN IP 10.100.23.10 and nft masquerade rule counters incrementing"},{"requirement":"mgmt/control-plane connectivity on node2/node3 left intact (not disrupted by the LAN routing change)","command_ids":["cmd-0afa6f52abec43af","cmd-b54f6b38c9894cc6","cmd-ae327d419d7844a3"],"summary":"ip route show default on node2/node3 continues to show the original DHCP default via enp1s0/10.100.23.1 unchanged after configuration and after reboot"},{"requirement":"Implemented using Ansible from the designated control_node","command_ids":["cmd-4604e4fbddf446e1","cmd-baff03e26a434bfe","cmd-f640e0d1ed8243b7","cmd-45a53e4ea2cc40b0","cmd-4c1c